                <pb facs="0813" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation (2)/263: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Costa
                        Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-12T18:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. Your 86, July 11, 11 a.m. If you have not already done so, please give the
                    Foreign Minister a copy of my statement in this regard as quoted in Radio
                    Bulletin No. 164, July 11.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
